    "lines": [
      {
        "y": 12.7,
        "x0": 33.2,
        "x1": 72.2,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "50"
      },
      {
        "y": 24.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 458.2,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "The news: gathering and delivering"
      },
      {
        "y": 70.7,
        "x0": 75.1,
        "x1": 207.4,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "A Gathering the news"
      },
      {
        "y": 130.8,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 227.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "NEWS TODAY"
      },
      {
        "y": 160.5,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 312.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "There are a number of different types of journalism: print"
      },
      {
        "y": 169.4,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 319.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "journalism1, broadcast journalism2, online journalism3—and,"
      },
      {
        "y": 179.8,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 332.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "increasingly, citizen journalism: this is where ordinary citizens use"
      },
      {
        "y": 189.5,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 323.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "social media to report, photograph and share news with others."
      },
      {
        "y": 202.3,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 332.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Professional journalists gather news in a number of different ways."
      },
      {
        "y": 211,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 334,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "They may get stories from pressure groups4 which want to air their"
      },
      {
        "y": 220.6,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 331.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "views5 in public. Journalists also attend press conferences6 where"
      },
      {
        "y": 230.2,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 345.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "politicians or others may issue a statement or press release7. A person"
      },
      {
        "y": 239.8,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 333.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "seeking publicity8 will try to include a soundbite9 in what they say."
      },
      {
        "y": 252.7,
        "x0": 111.5,
        "x1": 331.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Journalists also hunt for10 stories by tapping useful sources11 and"
      },
      {
        "y": 262.3,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 336.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "by monitoring12 international news agencies like Reuters. The more"
      },
      {
        "y": 271.9,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 336.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "important a story is, the more airtime13 it will achieve and the more"
      },
      {
        "y": 281.5,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 341.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "column inches14 it will be given in the newspaper or on the webpage:"
      },
      {
        "y": 291.1,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 341.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "in other words, the more coverage15 it will receive. Paparazzi16 follow"
      },
      {
        "y": 301.6,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 331,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "celebrities or public figures and try to get photographs of them for"
      },
      {
        "y": 311.2,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 205.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "newspapers and magazines."
      },
      {
        "y": 328.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 505.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 newspapers and magazines 2 radio and TV 3 news websites 4 people trying to influence what other"
      },
      {
        "y": 339.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 520.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "people think about a particular issue 5 express their opinions 6 meetings to give information to and answer"
      },
      {
        "y": 351.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 512.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "questions from the press 7 give a formal announcement to the press 8 wanting to reach a wider audience"
      },
      {
        "y": 362.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 484,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "9 short memorable sentence or phrase that will be repeated in news bulletins and articles 10 look for"
      },
      {
        "y": 374.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 507.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "11 making use of people or organisations which regularly provide news 12 regularly checking 13 minutes"
      },
      {
        "y": 385.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 515.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "given to it on radio or TV 14 space 15 media attention 16 an informal and sometimes disapproving word"
      },
      {
        "y": 398.2,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 189.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "for press photographers"
      },
      {
        "y": 414.8,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 208.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B Delivering the news"
      },
      {
        "y": 432.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 494.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "A rag is an informal word for a newspaper and it suggests that it is not of very high quality. The"
      },
      {
        "y": 444.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 498.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "gutter press is a disapproving term used about the kind of newspapers and magazines that are"
      },
      {
        "y": 456.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 316.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "more interested in crime and sex than serious news."
      },
      {
        "y": 468.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 500.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Journalists produce copy, which has to be ready for a deadline. With printed newspapers, when"
      },
      {
        "y": 480.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 307.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "everything is ready, the newspaper goes to press."
      },
      {
        "y": 492.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 520.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Previous issues of a paper are known as back copies. These are usually accessible in an online archive."
      },
      {
        "y": 504.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 521.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "A story that is only to be found in one newspaper is an exclusive or scoop. All newspapers or TV news"
      },
      {
        "y": 516.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 506.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "channels hope to run a story that no one else has discovered. A major story can be said to hit the"
      },
      {
        "y": 528.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 505.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "headlines on the day it is published. At that time, the story breaks or becomes public knowledge."
      },
      {
        "y": 540.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 504.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "A newspaper may be taken to court for libel or defamation of character if it publishes an untrue"
      },
      {
        "y": 552.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 371.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "story that, for example, wrongly accuses someone of something."
      },
      {
        "y": 564.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 505.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Journalists of different political persuasions will put their own gloss/spin on a story. [present it in"
      },
      {
        "y": 577.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 155.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "their own way]"
      },
      {
        "y": 588.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 377.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Some journalists gather stories by muck-raking. [collecting scandal]"
      },
      {
        "y": 600.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 499.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Generally, newspapers like to make stories sound more dramatic by using words like heroic and"
      },
      {
        "y": 612.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 416,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "triumph, even for some occurrence that is quite ordinary. [happening, event]"
      },
      {
        "y": 630.8,
        "x0": 110.7,
        "x1": 205,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Language help"
      },
      {
        "y": 654.6,
        "x0": 111.8,
        "x1": 504.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Media is a plural noun and should be used with a plural verb, e.g. The media are blamed for a number"
      },
      {
        "y": 666.6,
        "x0": 111.8,
        "x1": 497.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "of social problems. However, some people treat it as if it were a singular word, e.g. Social media has"
      },
      {
        "y": 678.9,
        "x0": 111.8,
        "x1": 487.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "had a huge impact on our lives. Media is often used as an adjective in phrases like media reports/"
      },
      {
        "y": 690.9,
        "x0": 111.8,
        "x1": 251.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "coverage/attention/interest/hype."
      }
    ],
